# The whole journey over HTTP: a seller lists an item, a second user bids, anyone reads the new price.
# Run the requests in order (VS Code REST Client syntax; one cookie jar, so each sign-up switches user).
# Start the stack first: docker compose -f deploy/compose.yaml up -d --wait api

@api = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Sign up the seller (DEMO_MODE: a display name and an email, signed in at once)
POST {{api}}/account/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Seller", "email": "seller-{{$guid}}@example.test" }

### 2. Create a draft: every term, amounts in cents, a hidden reserve of $15.00
# @name draft
POST {{api}}/auctions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "title": "Film camera",
  "description": "A 35 mm rangefinder in working order.",
  "openingPriceCents": 1000,
  "incrementCents": 100,
  "floorType": "reserve",
  "reserveCents": 1500,
  "bidEntry": "proxy",
  "startsAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "endsAt": "{{$datetime iso8601 1 h}}"
}

### 3. Publish it: the start time has passed, so it opens at once
POST {{api}}/auctions/{{draft.response.body.$.auctionId}}/publish
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

### 4. Sign up a buyer (this replaces the seller's session cookie)
POST {{api}}/account/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Buyer", "email": "buyer-{{$guid}}@example.test" }

### 5. Bid: a private maximum of $25.00 under proxy bidding
POST {{api}}/auctions/{{draft.response.body.$.auctionId}}/bids
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "amountCents": 2500 }

### 6. Read the price: $15.00, the reserve, reached because the maximum covers it; the maximum stays private
GET {{api}}/auctions/{{draft.response.body.$.auctionId}}

### 7. The bid history, with bidders shown only as labels
GET {{api}}/auctions/{{draft.response.body.$.auctionId}}/bids

### 8. The directory of published auctions, ending soonest first
GET {{api}}/auctions?pageSize=20
